---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="resume -- alexander campos" description="Alexander Campos - builds and ships agent memory and model routing, grounded in six years of regulated finance operations. Reframed (live), ForgeFrame (open source).">
  <article class="resume">
    <h1>Resume</h1>

    <ul class="stats" aria-label="At a glance">
      <li><b>6 yrs</b><span>regulated finance ops</span></li>
      <li><b>~80</b><span>people, SOP governance</span></li>
      <li><b>$600M+</b><span>regulatory network monitored</span></li>
      <li><b>78%</b><span>less manual review</span></li>
      <li><b>20,000+</b><span>account failure resolved solo</span></li>
      <li><b>$35B</b><span>merger, zero transmission errors</span></li>
      <li><b>50+ hrs</b><span>cut in one quarter</span></li>
    </ul>

    <section class="summary">
      <p>
        Six years in regulated bank operations, promoted four times in five years from a
        teller line to owning SOP governance and controls for an ~80-person department.
        Built the failure-driven monitoring behind a $600M+ regulatory network (78% less
        manual), resolved a 20,000-account logic failure solo, and drove zero transmission
        errors through a $35B merger integration. I build controls to multinational and
        national regulatory standards, and the automation that runs them without a person
        in the loop -- removing the work rather than staffing it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Skills</h2>

      <h3>Operations</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        SOP governance &amp; audits · Process modernization · Controls design ·
        Failure-surface monitoring · Dependency sequencing &amp; approval gates ·
        Metrics, KPIs &amp; executive reporting · Workflow automation · Change control ·
        Vendor operations
      </p>

      <h3>Regulated Environments</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        BSA/AML/KYC · SCRA · TILA/Reg Z · FDCPA/Reg F · NCUA · CFPB ·
        Systems integration &amp; onboarding
      </p>

      <h3>AI &amp; Data</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        Agents and automations running in production · Governed AI adoption
        (accelerant, not autopilot) · SQL (Postgres, Snowflake) · Python ·
        Splunk · Observe · Looker · Power BI · Tableau
      </p>

      <h3>Development</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        TypeScript · React · Node.js · Next.js · Astro · Electron · SQLite ·
        Python (Pandas, scikit-learn)
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Experience</h2>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <h3>Capital One -- Senior Process Manager, Card Legal Recoveries Operations</h3>
          <span class="dates">June 2025 -- Present | Richmond, VA</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Own the department's SOP governance function</strong> -- ~80 people
            across 8-9 teams. L5 SOP library, annual audits to the process-doc standard,
            ownership mapping, version history, and artifact change auditing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Stood up new controls and processes from the ground up</strong> to
            multinational and national regulatory standards across several regulatory
            bodies. Built with Engineering and the Data team, who validated each solution
            before it went live.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Run the controls loop on a $600M+ regulatory file-exchange network</strong>
            (300+ daily transmissions). Took anomaly detection from a rapid prototype to an
            automated pipeline, cutting manual monitoring 78% and turning every anomaly
            population into an identified control gap and a reconciled fix.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Built an automated business-review pipeline</strong> spanning six teams
            and 20+ operational data points. Consolidates into executive one-pagers that give
            senior leadership a noise-free read on what matters and why. It runs autonomously.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cut 50+ hours of manual work in a single quarter</strong> -- scripted
            automation across controls, process, monitoring, and analytics tasks.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Resolved a 20,000+ account logic failure</strong> independently while the
